%U A401994 2874274900856282558062061211,50294415688167961471109941793686,1767540926346422137530801523719834449
%N A401994 Number of digraphs on n unlabeled nodes, self-loops disallowed, that are reducible for every election of source-SCC headers.
%C A401994 The unlabeled counterpart of A401522. An election chooses one node from each source strongly connected component and joins a new root to all chosen nodes. Every such election must give a reducible flow graph. Each qualifying digraph is counted once up to isomorphism.
%C A401994 Equivalently, every source strongly connected component is reducible from each of its nodes, and every non-source component has one node receiving all incoming edges from other components and is reducible when rooted at that node. All digraphs have no self-loops.
%D A401994 F. Harary and E. M. Palmer, Graphical Enumeration, Academic Press, NY, 1973.
%D A401994 M. S. Hecht and J. D. Ullman, Flow graph reducibility, SIAM J. Comput. 1 (1972), 188-202.
%D A401994 M. S. Hecht and J. D. Ullman, Characterizations of reducible flow graphs, J. ACM 21 (1974), 367-375.
%D A401994 R. W. Robinson, Counting digraphs with restrictions on the strong components, in T.-H. Ku (ed.), Combinatorics and Graph Theory '95, World Scientific, Singapore, 1995, pp. 343-354.
%D A401994 R. E. Tarjan, Testing flow graph reducibility, J. Comput. System Sci. 9 (1974), 355-365.
%H A401994 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A401994/b401994.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..23</a>
%H A401994 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A397968/a397968.py.txt">Required Python module (unlabeled_reducible_cfgs.py)</a>, Aug 2026.
%H A401994 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A400123/a400123_1.py.txt">Required Python module (everywhere_reducible.py)</a>, Sep 2026.
%H A401994 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A398465/a398465.py.txt">Required Python module (labeled_reducible_cfgs.py)</a>, Jul 2026.
%H A401994 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A401321/a401321_1.py.txt">Required Python module (valid_header_elections.py)</a>, Oct 2026.
%H A401994 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A399885/a399885.py.txt">Python program (unlabeled_reducible_elections.py)</a>, Nov 2026.
%F A401994 a(n) = (1/n!) * Sum_{sigma in S_n} F_every(sigma), where F_every(sigma) is the number of loopless digraphs fixed by sigma for which every election of source-SCC headers is reducible.
%o A401994 (Python)
%o A401994 # Save the five linked Python files in one directory using the filenames
%o A401994 # shown in their link captions, then run Python in that directory.
